cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "scarcity-transition-sim"
abstract: >-
  A parametric agent-based simulation of seven economic coordination mechanisms
  (price signals, money, property rights, employment, taxation, reputation and
  queuing) as material scarcity declines from 1.0 to 0.0. Agents choose
  mechanisms through a large language model, and each mechanism is classified as
  collapsing, persisting or being repurposed.
authors:
  - family-names: "Lecomte"
    given-names: "Rodrigue"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rodlec888/scarcity-transition-sim"
keywords:
  - agent-based modeling
  - post-scarcity
  - economic coordination
  - large language models
  - Mesa
